# The Sword of Kahless: the quoted ability it grants is the Sword's text, so a text-changing effect on the Sword changes
# what the equipped creature's trigger looks for (CR 612.1, 113.7a), and the ability keeps those words once it has
# triggered, even after the Sword is gone (CR 113.7a, 608.2h). Artificial Evolution turns the Sword's "Warrior" into
# "Soldier"; the Bears attacks and Bot2 Shatters the Sword with the trigger on the stack. Among the top five, Alesha's
# Vanguard (an Orc Warrior) can't be chosen now, while Elite Vanguard (a Human Soldier) can and enters - alone: "a
# Klingon or Warrior creature card" is one, so it and Battle-Scarred Survivalist (a Klingon) together are refused. The Bears' own
# text is unchanged, so reading the creature's words, or the printed types, would get both wrong.

